a4:
  fun need<X, Y where X == Y>(x: X, y: Y) {}
  fun mk<E>() -> [E](let Void) -> Void { mk() }
  fun f<E>(p: [E](let Void) -> Void) { need(p, mk()) }
baseline: diagnostics 0. FIX and FULL: 1 diagnostic, "no coercion from '<X, Y> (X ~ Y) ==> ...' to '[Void](let [E](let Void) let -> Void, let [%6pv](let Void) let -> Void) let -> Void'".
Control a5, with the variable in an input instead of the environment: accepted in all 3 configurations.
semtest reports MISMATCH for a4 under FIX and FULL.
The baseline's own dump of need is '[Void](let [E]..., let [%dfl](let Void) let -> Void)'. Its acceptance therefore leaves an unresolved type variable in the elaboration, for the same root cause.

